{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 14: the market growth model with an anticipatory capacity policy (capacity ordered from forecast orders). Anticipate = 0 reproduces ch14-market-growth. }
Salespeople= INTEG(
	Sales Hiring,
	10)
	~	person
	~	Sales force.
	|
Sales Hiring=
	(Indicated Salespeople - Salespeople) / Hiring Time
	~	person/month
	~	Hiring (or release) towards the sales force the budget supports.
	|
Hiring Time=
	20
	~	month
	~	Time to adjust the sales force to the budget (Forrester 1968 uses 20 months).
	|
Indicated Salespeople=
	Sales Budget / Salesperson Salary
	~	person
	~	Sales force the budget can pay.
	|
Salesperson Salary=
	2000
	~	dollar/person/month
	~	Monthly cost of one salesperson.
	|
Sales Budget=
	Revenue * Budget Fraction
	~	dollar/month
	~	Revenue allocated to selling.
	|
Budget Fraction=
	0.1
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of revenue spent on the sales force.
	|
Revenue=
	Orders * Price
	~	dollar/month
	~	Revenue booked with orders.
	|
Price=
	100
	~	dollar/unit
	~	Revenue per unit ordered.
	|
Orders=
	Salespeople * Sales Effectiveness
	~	unit/month
	~	Orders booked.
	|
Sales Effectiveness=
	Normal Effectiveness * Delay Effect
	~	unit/person/month
	~	Orders per salesperson per month.
	|
Normal Effectiveness=
	400
	~	unit/person/month
	~	Orders per salesperson when delivery is immediate.
	|
Delay Effect=
	1 / (1 + (Market Delivery Delay / Half Effect Delay) ^ 3)
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of normal effectiveness kept at the delivery delay customers expect.
	|
Half Effect Delay=
	4
	~	month
	~	Delivery delay at which salespeople book half their normal orders.
	|
Market Delivery Delay=
	SMOOTH(Delivery Delay, Market Learning Time)
	~	month
	~	Delivery delay as customers know it.
	|
Market Learning Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Time for customers to learn the firm's delivery delay.
	|
Backlog= INTEG(
	Orders - Shipments,
	7111)
	~	unit
	~	Orders received but not yet shipped.
	|
Shipments=
	MIN(Capacity, Backlog / Minimum Delay)
	~	unit/month
	~	Shipments, limited by capacity or by the minimum processing time.
	|
Minimum Delay=
	1
	~	month
	~	Shortest possible time from order to shipment.
	|
Delivery Delay=
	Backlog / Shipments
	~	month
	~	Current delivery delay.
	|
Perceived Delivery Delay=
	SMOOTH(Delivery Delay, Reporting Time)
	~	month
	~	Delivery delay as management sees it in its reports.
	|
Reporting Time=
	3
	~	month
	~	Reporting and averaging time for the delivery delay.
	|
Traditional Goal=
	2
	~	month
	~	Delivery delay the company set as its standard.
	|
Weight on Tradition=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Weight of the traditional goal in the operating goal (0: goal follows performance; 1: firm goal).
	|
Goal Change=
	(Weight on Tradition * Traditional Goal + (1 - Weight on Tradition) * Perceived Delivery Delay - Delivery Delay Goal) / Goal Adjustment Time
	~	dmnl
	~	Drift of the operating goal towards a weighted mix of the traditional goal and the delivery delay management sees (months per month).
	|
Goal Adjustment Time=
	12
	~	month
	~	Time for the operating goal to drift towards experience.
	|
Delivery Delay Goal= INTEG(
	Goal Change,
	2)
	~	month
	~	Operating goal used to judge whether capacity is short.
	|
Delivery Condition=
	Perceived Delivery Delay / Delivery Delay Goal
	~	dmnl
	~	Above 1: deliveries are slower than the goal.
	|
Expansion Sensitivity=
	0.1
	~	1/month
	~	Capacity ordered per month, as a fraction of capacity, per unit of excess delivery condition.
	|
Expansion Fraction=
	MAX(0, Expansion Sensitivity * (Delivery Condition - 1))
	~	1/month
	~	Capacity ordered per month as a fraction of capacity in place.
	|
Anticipate=
	1
	~	dmnl
	~	1: order capacity from forecast orders; 0: from the delivery delay against its goal.
	|
Order Averaging Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Averaging time for the order trend.
	|
Average Orders=
	SMOOTH(Orders, Order Averaging Time)
	~	unit/month
	~	Smoothed order rate.
	|
Order Growth Rate=
	(Orders - Average Orders) / (Average Orders * Order Averaging Time)
	~	1/month
	~	Fractional growth of orders (first-order trend estimate).
	|
Forecast Orders=
	Orders * (1 + Order Growth Rate * Lead Time)
	~	unit/month
	~	Orders expected when capacity ordered now arrives.
	|
Target Utilisation=
	0.9
	~	dmnl
	~	Planned share of capacity used.
	|
Desired Capacity=
	Forecast Orders / Target Utilisation
	~	unit/month
	~	Capacity needed for forecast orders.
	|
Capacity Planning Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Time to close the gap between desired and planned capacity.
	|
Capacity Orders=
	MAX(0, (1 - Anticipate) * Capacity * Expansion Fraction + Anticipate * (Desired Capacity - Capacity - Capacity on Order) / Capacity Planning Time)
	~	unit/month/month
	~	New capacity ordered each month.
	|
Capacity on Order= INTEG(
	Capacity Orders - Capacity Arrivals,
	0)
	~	unit/month
	~	Capacity ordered but not yet producing.
	|
Lead Time=
	12
	~	month
	~	Average time to build and commission capacity.
	|
Capacity Arrivals=
	Capacity on Order / Lead Time
	~	unit/month/month
	~	Capacity coming on line.
	|
Capacity= INTEG(
	Capacity Arrivals,
	3556)
	~	unit/month
	~	Units the plant can ship per month.
	|
********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|
FINAL TIME  = 120
	~	month
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|
INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	month
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|
SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	month [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|
TIME STEP  = 0.125
	~	month [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|
